<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peloponnesian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">431–404 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Peloponnesian Wars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peloponnesian War was fought from 431 to 404 BCE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> and its empire and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-league">Peloponnesian League</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>. It ended in Athens' defeat. The war and the fractious alliances that followed weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-city-states">Greek city-states</a>, creating the conditions for the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war.jpg" alt="Peloponnesian War" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Translator was Kenmayer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pelop_war_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
